# --- DEEP 10-24 (the user: one hour per island - real height, a big climb, a deep dive): Standpipe Hill: a water tower on a forty-metre hill, a live flooded intake chamber, and a test pump that shows where the city's water really goes. ------
# the climb: the trail spirals up from the east foot; on the summit the old water tower (10 storeys, a ladder inside), its deck chest
# and a zipline down to the hub (the shortcut back); the dive: the flooded intake chamber on a basin floor -16 m down, an air pocket
# in its front room; the hub: the Test-pump lever that wants both, the notice; secrets: the trail ledge cache, the summit treasure,
# the sunk boat's crate
call hw_zone x=-8.14 z=-2.54 al=pc_trailz id=pc_trail r=5 msg="The trail up Standpipe Hill starts here - cut into the slope, round and up."
call hw_zone x=-32 z=-10 al=pc_summitz id=pc_summit r=8 h=1 msg="The top of Standpipe Hill. The whole island below, the city beyond it, and the old water tower still higher."
call hw_mast x=-31.28 z=-6.06 h0=38 lv=10 a=pc_mast chest=pc_topchest top=Placeable_WaterTank
place ZiplinePath_Landmark pc_zip at -29.68 -13.44 h=39.35
zipto pc_zip -39.28 -50.06
place Loot_ChestSmall pc_ledge at -40.2 -18.9 ground sit yaw=42.65
call treasure x=-35.94 z=-9.28 r=5 n=1 seed=13578 kind=0
prop treasure13578 treasure.loot=CopperOre*2;MetalOre*2;TradeToken*1
